From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:31:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mpg4c32: Add a Microsoft MPEG-4 Video for Windows decoder.

Games which play MS-MPEG4 (MP42, MP43) AVIs through AVIFile /
AVIStreamGetFrame need a Video for Windows codec: Wine has none for
these formats, ICLocate finds no decompressor and AVIStreamGetFrameOpen
fails. Powerboat GT's DirectorAVI.dll then dereferences the NULL frame
and the game crashes at its boat selection videos (MP42, written by
ffdshow, stream handler "ffds").

Add mpg4c32.dll, the name of Windows' MPEG-4 VCM, on the model of
ir50_32: the ICM driver decodes through winedmo's WMVideo decoder MFT,
which already handles MP42 (0102) and MP43 (0066). It is registered
as vidc.MP42 and vidc.MP43; ICLocate's driver enumeration finds it for
any stream handler.

The decoder is created through a new winedmo export,
winedmo_create_wmv_decoder(), as ir50_32 does with
winedmo_create_video_decoder(). wmvdecod.dll's class factory only
forwards to CoCreateInstance(), which fails on a game thread that has
not initialized COM (unless the process already has an MTA).

[GloriousEggroll: create the decoder through a winedmo export instead
of wmvdecod.dll's COM class factory]

Tested with Powerboat GT: its boat videos play, the game reaches the
race (tested before the switch to winedmo_create_wmv_decoder()).
